% Orthopedic Footwear: LCD L33641 and its Policy Article A52481 (DME MACs).
% A policy program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le (orders,
% delivery, benefit category, continued need, refills) and states when a
% claim for an orthopedic shoe, an insert or modification, a heel or sole
% replacement, a shoe transfer or a prosthetic shoe is REASONABLE AND
% NECESSARY:
%   - Oxford shoes (L3224, L3225) that are an integral part of a covered leg
%     brace (the Article's brace codes L1900, L1920, L1980, L1990, L2000,
%     L2005, L2010, L2020, L2030, L2050, L2060, L2080, L2090);
%   - other shoes (L3649), inserts and other shoe modifications (the
%     Article's L3000–L3595 list) on such a shoe, when medically necessary
%     for the proper functioning of the brace;
%   - heel and sole replacements (L3455, L3460, L3530, L3540) and shoe
%     transfers (L3600–L3640) involving shoes on a covered brace;
%   - prosthetic shoes (L3250), the LCD's one criterion: an integral part of
%     a prosthesis (the shoe holds a removable custom fabricated insert for a
%     toe or distal partial foot amputation) for a beneficiary with a partial
%     foot amputation — the Article's ICD-10 table
%     (sources/icd10/A52481_icd10_covered.csv, loaded as the table
%     orthopedic_footwear_icd10; its one group, group 1, serves L3250) —
%     and not put on over another lower limb prosthesis.
% Every other footwear code the Article lists (a matching shoe not
% attached to a brace, a shoe billed apart from its brace) is statutorily
% excluded: no rule concludes it. Whether a shoe is part of a brace decides
% the benefit itself ("coverage is statutorily excluded"), but dmepos.le
% decides the benefit by code: the codes are placed in the benefit, and the
% Article's condition is read here in section question, with its passages.
% The foot pressure off-loading device (A9283) has no benefit category at
% all. The benefit is not durable medical equipment: the Policy Article
% places orthopedic footwear under the leg, arm, back, and neck braces, and
% artificial legs, arms and eyes benefit (Social Security Act §1861(s)(9)).
%
% How the criteria are read. What the record states is a scenario fact:
% the shoe is an integral part of a brace (attached to it), the brace is a
% covered leg brace — the brace's own claim is decided by the AFO/KAFO
% policy (afo_kafo.le), so here it is a fact of the record rather than a
% conclusion (including afo_kafo.le would put its documentation rule, which
% fails on every footwear claim, in the way of "stage") —, an insert or a
% heel is an accessory of its shoe (the shared template), the prosthetic
% shoe holds its partial foot insert, the diagnosis code. One criterion is
% a judgment, the judged template of dmepos.le:
%   footwear necessary for brace function (L3649, inserts and
%   modifications: "medically necessary for the proper functioning of the
%   brace").
%
% The payment conditions the Policy Article adds ("Policy specific
% documentation requirements", "Modifiers"), in section remedy: the
% diagnosis code on each claim for a prosthetic shoe; for L3649 a narrative
% description of the item and a statement of its medical necessity on the
% claim. The Article also exempts heel and sole replacements and shoe
% transfers from the order ("An order is not required"): a rule of this
% program for dmepos.le's "the order requirements are met for an item",
% guarded by those codes.
%
% Not modelled: the KX, GY, RT and LT modifiers; that the brace's supplier
% bills its shoes; the therapeutic shoes for diabetics (another policy,
% therapeutic_shoes.le).

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    *an item* is an integral part of *a device*; undefined.
    *a device* is a covered leg brace; undefined.
    *an item* holds a removable custom fabricated insert for a partial foot amputation; undefined.
    % candidate for dmepos.le (also a template of afo_kafo.le and knee_orthoses.le)
    *a claim* states the diagnosis code of the beneficiary; undefined.
    *a claim* describes *an item* with a statement of its medical necessity; undefined.
    % the codes and the table
    ICD10 code *a code* is in group *a group* of article *an article* as *a description* under table orthopedic_footwear_icd10.
    code *a code* is excluded from the braces benefit of orthopedic footwear.
    % derived
    *an item* is a leg brace of the footwear policy.
    *an item* is a shoe modification.
    *an item* is a shoe repair item.
    *a shoe* is on a covered leg brace.
    *a beneficiary* has a partial foot amputation.
    *an item* is put on over another lower limb prosthesis.
    the prosthetic shoe diagnosis requirement is met for *a claim*.
    the narrative requirement is met for *a claim*.

% The Article's ICD-10 table: the partial foot amputations and congenital
% absences (group 1, the only group, serving L3250; the CSV columns bind to
% the template's arguments in order: code, group, article, description).
the table orthopedic_footwear_icd10 is loaded from sources/icd10/A52481_icd10_covered.csv, with all matches:
    code | group | article | description

the knowledge base orthopedic_footwear includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base orthopedic_footwear includes:

LCD L33641 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33641".
the text of LCD L33641 is at "sources/lcd/L33641.txt".
Policy Article A52481 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52481".
the text of Policy Article A52481 is at "sources/article/A52481.txt".

% What the items are, by code (Policy Article A52481).
rule footwear_braces with provenance Policy Article A52481,
        confer "Shoes are also covered if they are an integral part of a covered leg brace described by codes L1900, L1920, L1980, L1990 , L2000, L2005, L2010, L2020, L2030, L2050, L2060, L2080, or L2090":
an item is a leg brace of the footwear policy
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L1900", "L1920", "L1980", "L1990", "L2000", "L2005", "L2010", "L2020", "L2030", "L2050", "L2060", "L2080", "L2090"].

% An insert is one of the shoe modifications ("Inserts and other shoe
% modifications"); heel and sole replacements and shoe transfers are the
% shoe repair items.
rule footwear_inserts with provenance Policy Article A52481,
        confer "are covered if they are on a shoe that is an integral part of a covered brace and if they are medically necessary for the proper functioning of the brace":
an item is a shoe modification
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L3000", "L3001", "L3002", "L3003", "L3010", "L3020", "L3030", "L3031", "L3040", "L3050", "L3060", "L3070", "L3080", "L3090", "L3100", "L3140", "L3150", "L3160", "L3170", "L3300", "L3310", "L3320", "L3330", "L3332", "L3334", "L3340", "L3350", "L3360", "L3370", "L3380", "L3390", "L3400", "L3410", "L3420", "L3430", "L3440", "L3450", "L3465", "L3470", "L3480", "L3485", "L3500", "L3510", "L3520", "L3550", "L3560", "L3570", "L3580", "L3590", "L3595"].

rule footwear_repairs with provenance Policy Article A52481,
        confer "Heel replacements (L3455, L3460), sole replacements (L3530, L3540), and shoe transfers (L3600, L3610, L3620, L3630 and L3640) involving shoes on a covered brace are also covered":
an item is a shoe repair item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L3455", "L3460", "L3530", "L3540", "L3600", "L3610", "L3620", "L3630", "L3640"].

section applicability is:

% The codes this policy decides: the footwear codes of the Article, and the
% off-loading device it denies.
rule footwear_codes with provenance Policy Article A52481,
        confer "With the exception of the situations described above, orthopedic footwear billed using codes":
the policy for code a code is orthopedic_footwear
    if the code is in ["L3000", "L3001", "L3002", "L3003", "L3010", "L3020", "L3030", "L3031", "L3040", "L3050", "L3060", "L3070", "L3080", "L3090", "L3100", "L3140", "L3150", "L3160", "L3170", "L3201", "L3202", "L3203", "L3204", "L3206", "L3207", "L3208", "L3209", "L3211", "L3212", "L3213", "L3214", "L3215", "L3216", "L3217", "L3219", "L3221", "L3222", "L3224", "L3225", "L3230", "L3250", "L3251", "L3252", "L3253", "L3254", "L3255", "L3257", "L3260", "L3265", "L3300", "L3310", "L3320", "L3330", "L3332", "L3334", "L3340", "L3350", "L3360", "L3370", "L3380", "L3390", "L3400", "L3410", "L3420", "L3430", "L3440", "L3450", "L3455", "L3460", "L3465", "L3470", "L3480", "L3485", "L3500", "L3510", "L3520", "L3530", "L3540", "L3550", "L3560", "L3570", "L3580", "L3590", "L3595", "L3600", "L3610", "L3620", "L3630", "L3640", "L3649", "A9283"].

% The benefit: the braces and artificial limbs benefit of Social Security
% Act §1861(s)(9) — for every code but the off-loading device.
rule footwear_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52481,
        confer "Orthopedic footwear is covered under the leg, arm, back, and neck braces, and artificial legs, arms and eyes benefit (Social Security Act §1861(s)(9))":
the benefit category of code a code is "leg, arm, back, and neck braces, and artificial legs, arms and eyes"
    if the policy for code the code is orthopedic_footwear
    and it is not the case that
        code the code is excluded from the braces benefit of orthopedic footwear.

code "A9283" is excluded from the braces benefit of orthopedic footwear,
    as stated in Policy Article A52481, confer "A foot pressure off-loading/ supportive device (A9283) is denied as noncovered because there is no Medicare benefit category for these items".

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Shoes on a brace, and what goes on them.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule footwear_oxford with provenance Policy Article A52481,
        confer "Oxford shoes (L3224, L3225) are covered in these situations":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L3224", "L3225"]
    and the item is on a covered leg brace.

rule footwear_other_shoes with provenance Policy Article A52481,
        confer "Other shoes, e.g. high top, depth inlay or custom for non-diabetics, etc. (L3649), are also covered if they are an integral part of a covered brace and if they are medically necessary for the proper functioning of the brace":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "L3649"
    and the item is on a covered leg brace
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the finding footwear necessary for brace function about the beneficiary is established.

rule footwear_inserts_covered with provenance Policy Article A52481,
        confer "are covered if they are on a shoe that is an integral part of a covered brace and if they are medically necessary for the proper functioning of the brace":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a shoe modification
    and the item is an accessory of a shoe
    and the shoe is on a covered leg brace
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the finding footwear necessary for brace function about the beneficiary is established.

rule footwear_repairs_covered with provenance Policy Article A52481,
        confer "Heel replacements (L3455, L3460), sole replacements (L3530, L3540), and shoe transfers (L3600, L3610, L3620, L3630 and L3640) involving shoes on a covered brace are also covered":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a shoe repair item
    and the item is an accessory of a shoe
    and the shoe is on a covered leg brace.

rule footwear_on_brace with provenance Policy Article A52481,
        confer "According to a national policy determination, a shoe and related modifications, inserts, and heel/sole replacements, are covered only when the shoe is an integral part of a brace":
a shoe is on a covered leg brace
    if the shoe is an integral part of a device
    and the device is a leg brace of the footwear policy
    and the device is a covered leg brace.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Prosthetic shoes.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule footwear_prosthetic_shoe with provenance LCD L33641,
        confer "Prosthetic shoes (L3250) are covered if they are an integral part of a prosthesis for a beneficiary with a partial foot amputation":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "L3250"
    and the item holds a removable custom fabricated insert for a partial foot amputation
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary has a partial foot amputation
    and it is not the case that
        the item is put on over another lower limb prosthesis.

rule footwear_partial_foot with provenance LCD L33641,
        confer "Claims for prosthetic shoes for other diagnosis codes will be denied as not medically necessary":
a beneficiary has a partial foot amputation
    if the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and ICD10 code the code is in group 1 of article "A52481" as a description under table orthopedic_footwear_icd10.

rule footwear_over_prosthesis with provenance Policy Article A52481,
        confer "Code L3250 must not be used for a shoe that is put on other types of leg prostheses":
an item is put on over another lower limb prosthesis
    if the item is an integral part of a device
    and the HCPCS code of the device is a code
    and the code is in ["L5010", "L5020", "L5050", "L5060", "L5100", "L5105", "L5150", "L5160", "L5200", "L5210", "L5220", "L5230", "L5250", "L5270", "L5280", "L5301", "L5312", "L5321", "L5331", "L5341", "L5400", "L5410", "L5420", "L5430", "L5450", "L5460", "L5500", "L5505", "L5510", "L5520", "L5530", "L5535", "L5540", "L5560", "L5570", "L5580", "L5585", "L5590", "L5595", "L5600"].

section remedy is:

% The policy's own conditions of payment (Policy Article A52481).
rule footwear_documentation with provenance Policy Article A52481,
        confer "POLICY SPECIFIC DOCUMENTATION REQUIREMENTS":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is orthopedic_footwear
    and the prosthetic shoe diagnosis requirement is met for the claim
    and the narrative requirement is met for the claim.

rule footwear_diagnosis_on_claim with provenance Policy Article A52481,
        confer "When billing for prosthetic shoes (L3250) and related items, diagnosis code(s) to the highest level of specificity describing the condition which necessitates the prosthetic shoes, must be included on each claim for the prosthetic shoes and related items":
the prosthetic shoe diagnosis requirement is met for a claim
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "L3250"
    and the claim states the diagnosis code of the beneficiary.

% any other code: a device of this model
rule footwear_no_diagnosis_requirement:
the prosthetic shoe diagnosis requirement is met for a claim
    if the claim is for an item
    and it is not the case that
        the HCPCS code of the item is "L3250".

rule footwear_narrative with provenance Policy Article A52481,
        confer "When code L3649 with a KX modifier is billed, the claim must include a narrative description of the item provided as well as a brief statement of the medical necessity for the item":
the narrative requirement is met for a claim
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "L3649"
    and the claim describes the item with a statement of its medical necessity.

% any other code: a device of this model
rule footwear_no_narrative_requirement:
the narrative requirement is met for a claim
    if the claim is for an item
    and it is not the case that
        the HCPCS code of the item is "L3649".

% No order for a heel or sole replacement or a shoe transfer: the Article's
% exception to the order requirements of dmepos.le.
rule footwear_no_order_needed with provenance Policy Article A52481,
        confer "An order is not required for a heel or sole replacement or transfer of a shoe to a brace":
the order requirements are met for an item
    if the item is a shoe repair item.
